    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29538" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŏnaulos</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŏnaulus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόναυλος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a single flute, a
				flute with a single pipe</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fistulam et monaulum (invenit) Pan Mercurii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 56, 57, § 204</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saepe monaulon habet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 14, 64, 2</span></i>
			; cf. monaules.</div>
